        "original_id": "e5ad2f70-b7b6-5d67-9b17-e928cf875f8d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Kuvasz, Bouvier des Ardennes, Maremma Sheepdog, Pyrenean Mountain Dog, Tatra, Cuvac, Šarplaninac, Akbash Dog\n- Places: Hungary, Belgium, Poland, Slovakia, Turkey\n- Concepts: dog breeds, livestock dogs, common ancestry\n\nFacts:\n- The Kuvasz is an ancient breed of livestock dog of Hungarian origin.\n- The Bouvier des Ardennes is a rare dog breed from Belgium.\n- The Maremma Sheepdog is described as similar to the Pyrenean Mountain Dog, the Kuvasz of Hungary, the Tatra of Poland, the Cuvac of Slovakia, the Šarplaninac, and the Akbash Dog of Turkey.\n- The Maremma Sheepdog and the Pyrenean Mountain Dog, Kuvasz, Tatra, Cuvac, and Šarplaninac may share a common ancestor.\n- The Šarplaninac is noted as not white in the comparison of breeds similar to the Maremma Sheepdog.",
